{"id":"n5-107","title":"どこへも Verb ません","romaji":"doko e mo + Verb + masen","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Nowhere; Not to any place","longExplanation":"The grammar point どこへも is used to express the idea of 'nowhere' or 'not to any place'. It is combined with the negative form of a verb to indicate that the action does not happen to any place or destination.","formation":"どこへも + Verb-negative","examples":[{"jp":"今日はどこへも行きません。","romaji":"Kyou wa doko e mo ikimasen.","en":"I won't go anywhere today.","words":[{"surface":"今日","vocabId":"1579110","reading":"きょう"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"どこ","vocabId":"1577140","reading":"どこ"},{"surface":"へ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"も","vocabId":null},{"surface":"行き","vocabId":"1578790","reading":"いき","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2,3,4]},{"jp":"彼はどこへも走りませんでした。","romaji":"Kare wa doko e mo hashirimasen deshita.","en":"He didn't run anywhere.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"どこ","vocabId":"1577140","reading":"どこ"},{"surface":"へ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"も","vocabId":null},{"surface":"走り","vocabId":"1402420","reading":"はしり","baseForm":"走る"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"でし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"です"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2,3,4]},{"jp":"どこへも買い物に行きませんでした。","romaji":"Doko e mo kaimono ni ikimasen deshita.","en":"I didn't go shopping anywhere.","words":[{"surface":"どこ","vocabId":"1577140","reading":"どこ"},{"surface":"へ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"も","vocabId":null},{"surface":"買い物","vocabId":"1589730","reading":"かいもの"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"行き","vocabId":"1578790","reading":"いき","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surfac